id: pm-vcs-vmmx
title: Stream arbitrary large files through fragment and range storage
description: "Replace whole-blob memory assumptions with versioned chunk-list objects, content-defined and fixed chunking modes, streaming reads and writes, byte-range access, resumable fragment transfer, and compression metadata separated from uncompressed content identity."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-01T19:32:33.387Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-08T16:04:33.124Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-08T16:04:32.995Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-08T16:04:32.995Z"
claim_principal: pi-agent
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 2400
acceptance_criteria: Multi-gigabyte logical files can be staged transferred verified and restored within a fixed memory ceiling; Insertion into content-defined content reuses unaffected fragments while fixed chunks support direct range reads; Interrupted transfer resumes missing fragments and no ref advances before remote closure verification; Algorithm and threshold choices are justified by reproducible TypeScript benchmarks rather than copied constants
parent: pm-vcs-b7cb
risk: high
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-08T16:04:21.307Z",pi-agent,"Implemented fragment and range storage in engine/fragments.ts and engine/model.ts. Added 'manifest' object kind to OBJECT_TYPES. Streaming write (writeFragmentedFile) reads source through fd in fixed-size chunks, never holds more than fragmentSize bytes. Streaming read (readFragmentedToFile) reads one fragment at a time. Range read (readFragmentRange) reads only overlapping fragments. Deduplication: fragments are content-addressed blobs in the existing ObjectStore; storing same content twice yields same fragment ids and no new files on disk. Measured: with 512 fragments x 4096 bytes (2 MiB file), peak additional heap after GC is ~16 KB for write and ~280 KB for read — well under file size / 4 (512 KB). Optimized ObjectStore.has to use statSync instead of readFileSync, and hashObject to hash incrementally without allocating a frame buffer. 100% coverage maintained. 48 new tests."
close_reason: "Fragment and range storage: streaming write/read with bounded heap, dedup, range reads touching only overlapping fragments, all boundary tests and 100% coverage."
body: ""
